{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will establish My covenant</b> as a sign that HaShem swore to him that he and his sons would not die in the flood. And if it is not found explicitly at first, as we found in the Mishneh Torah \"Let us send men before us\" (Deuteronomy 1:22) — and the word והקימותי means \"I will fulfill My oath.\" And it seems likely to me that this covenant alludes to the rainbow. And the meaning of ברית is an agreement and a matter chosen by two parties; it is from the root of ברו לכם איש (1 Samuel 17:8). And the word is the same whether in construct state or absolute: thus שְבִת יעקב (Psalms 85:2) and ובנותיו בשבית (Numbers 21:29). And some say: a covenant of a cut boundary."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The citation from Numbers gives בשבית where the Masoretic text reads בשבי; retained Ibn Ezra's spelling as transmitted."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:33.286718860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}